Mupa is an original clean-room implementation. It depends on the following
open-source libraries and tools:

1. AndroidX (Core, Activity, Lifecycle, Navigation, DataStore, Compose,
   Material3, SplashScreen, Media3 ExoPlayer/Session/DataSource, ProfileInstaller)
   License: Apache License 2.0
   https://source.android.com/

2. Kotlin Standard Library, Kotlinx Coroutines, Kotlinx Serialization
   License: Apache License 2.0
   https://kotlinlang.org/

3. Dagger / Hilt
   License: Apache License 2.0
   https://dagger.dev/hilt/

4. OkHttp & Coil
   License: Apache License 2.0
   https://square.github.io/okhttp/
   https://coil-kt.github.io/coil/

5. NewPipeExtractor (isolated inside :streaming:innertube for stream cipher/n-param resolution)
   License: GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later)
   https://github.com/TeamNewPipe/NewPipeExtractor

6. Rust Local Engine Crates (engine/local-rust/)
